{"id": "H-014", "type": "multi", "retrieved": [{"rank": 1, "id": "ehds.pdf:p31:c6", "file": "ehds.pdf", "page": 31, "score": 0.813429}, {"rank": 2, "id": "gdpr.pdf:p34:c4", "file": "gdpr.pdf", "page": 34, "score": 0.789016}, {"rank": 3, "id": "ehds.pdf:p31:c0", "file": "ehds.pdf", "page": 31, "score": 0.788266}, {"rank": 4, "id": "ehds.pdf:p31:c5", "file": "ehds.pdf", "page": 31, "score": 0.777193}, {"rank": 5, "id": "ehds.pdf:p1:c2", "file": "ehds.pdf", "page": 1, "score": 0.760906}, {"rank": 6, "id": "ehds.pdf:p2:c4", "file": "ehds.pdf", "page": 2, "score": 0.760733}, {"rank": 7, "id": "ehds.pdf:p73:c0", "file": "ehds.pdf", "page": 73, "score": 0.758259}, {"rank": 8, "id": "ehds.pdf:p32:c2", "file": "ehds.pdf", "page": 32, "score": 0.757885}, {"rank": 9, "id": "ehds.pdf:p21:c5", "file": "ehds.pdf", "page": 21, "score": 0.755275}, {"rank": 10, "id": "ehds.pdf:p32:c0", "file": "ehds.pdf", "page": 32, "score": 0.754846}], "latency_s": 7.881, "answer": "The EHDS defines 'personal electronic health data' as data concerning health and genetic data, processed in an electronic form. This aligns with the GDPR's definition of 'data concerning health', which includes personal data related to the physical or mental health of a natural person, including the provision of healthcare services that reveal information about their health status. The EHDS also covers non-personal electronic health data, which are electronic health data other than personal electronic health data and include anonymised data no longer relating to an identified or identifiable natural person. This builds on GDPR's broader definition by specifying types of personal data related to health and genetic characteristics that can be processed in an electronic form.", "refused": false, "error": null, "source_ids": ["ehds.pdf:p31:c6", "gdpr.pdf:p34:c4", "ehds.pdf:p31:c0", "ehds.pdf:p31:c5", "ehds.pdf:p1:c2", "ehds.pdf:p2:c4", "ehds.pdf:p73:c0", "ehds.pdf:p32:c2", "ehds.pdf:p21:c5", "ehds.pdf:p32:c0"]}
{"id": "H-015", "type": "multi", "retrieved": [{"rank": 1, "id": "ehds.pdf:p5:c1", "file": "ehds.pdf", "page": 5, "score": 0.766959}, {"rank": 2, "id": "gdpr.pdf:p12:c6", "file": "gdpr.pdf", "page": 12, "score": 0.762587}, {"rank": 3, "id": "ehds.pdf:p4:c11", "file": "ehds.pdf", "page": 4, "score": 0.760821}, {"rank": 4, "id": "ehds.pdf:p5:c0", "file": "ehds.pdf", "page": 5, "score": 0.755479}, {"rank": 5, "id": "ehds.pdf:p37:c1", "file": "ehds.pdf", "page": 37, "score": 0.746923}, {"rank": 6, "id": "ehds.pdf:p36:c0", "file": "ehds.pdf", "page": 36, "score": 0.745854}, {"rank": 7, "id": "ehds.pdf:p34:c3", "file": "ehds.pdf", "page": 34, "score": 0.741424}, {"rank": 8, "id": "ehds.pdf:p3:c2", "file": "ehds.pdf", "page": 3, "score": 0.739168}, {"rank": 9, "id": "ehds.pdf:p63:c7", "file": "ehds.pdf", "page": 63, "score": 0.739075}, {"rank": 10, "id": "ehds.pdf:p3:c8", "file": "ehds.pdf", "page": 3, "score": 0.738234}], "latency_s": 8.229, "answer": "Yes, your country could hold back a worrying test result from your online health record until a doctor has explained it to you. This is allowed by Article 8 of the EHDS Regulation, which permits natural persons to restrict access to their personal electronic health data for a limited period if necessary to protect natural persons on the basis of patient safety and ethical considerations.\n\nGDPR Rule: The right to restrict processing under GDPR (Article 21) allows individuals to prevent certain types of processing. However, this is not directly applicable as it pertains more broadly to all personal data rather than specifically to health data in the EHDS context. For health data within the scope of the EHDS Regulation, the specific Article 8 right applies.", "refused": false, "error": null, "source_ids": ["ehds.pdf:p5:c1", "gdpr.pdf:p12:c6", "ehds.pdf:p4:c11", "ehds.pdf:p5:c0", "ehds.pdf:p37:c1", "ehds.pdf:p36:c0", "ehds.pdf:p34:c3", "ehds.pdf:p3:c2", "ehds.pdf:p63:c7", "ehds.pdf:p3:c8"]}
{"id": "H-016", "type": "multi", "retrieved": [{"rank": 1, "id": "ehds.pdf:p82:c0", "file": "ehds.pdf", "page": 82, "score": 0.810084}, {"rank": 2, "id": "ehds.pdf:p82:c3", "file": "ehds.pdf", "page": 82, "score": 0.75863}, {"rank": 3, "id": "ehds.pdf:p24:c11", "file": "ehds.pdf", "page": 24, "score": 0.757131}, {"rank": 4, "id": "ehds.pdf:p83:c0", "file": "ehds.pdf", "page": 83, "score": 0.755609}, {"rank": 5, "id": "ehds.pdf:p28:c3", "file": "ehds.pdf", "page": 28, "score": 0.747975}, {"rank": 6, "id": "gdpr.pdf:p87:c2", "file": "gdpr.pdf", "page": 87, "score": 0.746684}, {"rank": 7, "id": "ehds.pdf:p82:c1", "file": "ehds.pdf", "page": 82, "score": 0.745747}, {"rank": 8, "id": "ehds.pdf:p3:c0", "file": "ehds.pdf", "page": 3, "score": 0.745603}, {"rank": 9, "id": "ehds.pdf:p83:c2", "file": "ehds.pdf", "page": 83, "score": 0.743999}, {"rank": 10, "id": "ehds.pdf:p19:c6", "file": "ehds.pdf", "page": 19, "score": 0.739214}], "latency_s": 5.331, "answer": "No information provided about a research institute applying for EHDS health data. The general GDPR principle governing sending personal data to non-EU countries is the necessity and proportionality principle. However, specific conditions apply based on adequacy decisions or other criteria as per Article 45 of Regulation (EU) 2016/679.", "refused": false, "error": null, "source_ids": ["ehds.pdf:p82:c0", "ehds.pdf:p82:c3", "ehds.pdf:p24:c11", "ehds.pdf:p83:c0", "ehds.pdf:p28:c3", "gdpr.pdf:p87:c2", "ehds.pdf:p82:c1", "ehds.pdf:p3:c0", "ehds.pdf:p83:c2", "ehds.pdf:p19:c6"]}
